{
  "row": {
    "id": 17,
    "scenario": "Re-point while writing; a re-point interrupted and finished at boot; purge; factory reset; adopt by project id; config reset",
    "required_outcome": "Re-point refused while a write is pending, then done; the partition keeps its key, its snapshot and its notes under the new path; a re-point interrupted after any step is finished by the next boot; purge keeps memory; a factory reset orphans but never reassigns, and leaves projects/, the snapshots and the index; adopt finds each project partition by its project id; config reset keeps the owner"
  },
  "design": [
    "storage design §5 R18: a project partition's key is proj-<owner-key>-<16 hex of sha256(project id)>; its snapshot binds by project id and its root is never compared",
    "storage design §6 Re-point, steps 1-4, and R24: a project.json carrying previous_root is finished at boot, each step idempotent",
    "storage design §5 R20: adopt finds a project partition's folder by the id in its snapshot; R22: a snapshot with no id is listed, never opened, adopted or deleted",
    "memory design §2 and storage design §8: a factory reset does not touch memory or projects/ — state/memory-control/, the index and projects/<name>/ survive",
    "memory design §3 Resets: a plain config reset must not delete identity.*; a factory reset mints a new owner; doctor lists the orphans; adopt re-binds"
  ],
  "loads_in": ["slice-3"],
  "notes_for_implementer": "No loader runs this file; it is pinned by hand-written tests. Steps 1-5 (a re-point refused while a write of the project is pending, then done; the partition keeps its key, snapshot file and note under the new path): routes::workspaces::tests::a_repoint_keeps_the_projects_memory_under_its_key and memory::service::tests::a_repointed_projects_notes_keep_their_key_revision_and_index_rows. Steps 6-10 (a re-point stopped after step 1, then after step 3, finished by the next boot): memory_files::tests::a_repoint_interrupted_after_any_step_keeps_the_partition_once_recovered, with S3's project_life recovery tests. Step 11 and step 16 (the doctor): memory_files::tests::doctor_finds_a_repointed_partition_by_id_and_lists_an_idless_snapshot. Step 12 purges project_d, a project no later step names, so whatever the purge does to memory changes no later expectation; S5a rewrites step 12 as the delete (ST-19: every owner's notes and projects/<name>/ go). Steps 13-15 and 23-24 are the reset rows of the slice-3 fixture: the factory reset deletes only the database and the two config files (apps/openalpaca config_factory_reset tests). Steps 17-22 (adopt refused on a collision, then adopting by project id after three re-points): memory_files::tests::adopt_after_a_repoint_finds_the_partition_by_its_project_id, adopt_refuses_the_whole_command_on_one_collision, and the CLI's repair_lifts_a_quarantine_and_adopt_rebinds_an_orphan. The re-point's crash hook is project_life::repoint_with; `crash_after_step` names RepointStep 1 Marked, 2 RowsRewritten, 3 Renamed.",
